      <h2>Before you file</h2>

      <p>Assemble a claim packet containing the contract, change orders, claimant ledger, known owner-payment records, delivery tickets or daily reports, deed/legal description, Notice of Commencement, preliminary notices, mailing proof, and deadline calculation. That packet supports both accurate preparation and a fast response to a contest.</p>

      <p>Use a <a href="/lien-waiver/conditional/">conditional lien waiver</a> when payment has been promised but has not cleared. Once the secured debt is satisfied, record the appropriate <a href="/mechanics-lien/release/">mechanics lien release</a>.</p>

      <p><em>This page is general information, not legal advice. Georgia lien statutes are technical, deadlines may be shortened, and project facts matter. Verify current law and consult a Georgia construction attorney when rights or substantial sums are at risk.</em></p>

